2026-10-11T05:40:25.3453328Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3540278Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3548949Z [0m
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3549473Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3549996Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3550166Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3550747Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3551411Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3551743Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3552051Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3552521Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3552739Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3553272Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3554092Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3554652Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3555069Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3555234Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3555431Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3555635Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3555843Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3556151Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3556432Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3556538Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3556663Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3556951Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3557351Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3560270Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3560386Z I will:
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3560531Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3560763Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3561272Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3561667Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3561983Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3562210Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3562434Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3562874Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3563174Z    /root
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3634469Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3635093Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3649922Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3650786Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3651348Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3651900Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3652554Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3662969Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3663878Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3672827Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3673609Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3673987Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3674144Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3674320Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3674610Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3674925Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3675451Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3675629Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3675737Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3675975Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676123Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676313Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676595Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676709Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676719Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3676916Z [32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
2026-10-11T05:40:25.3683788Z [0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
